,"person_slug":"mark-banasiak","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Mark Buttigieg","person_id":"nsw_2253","person_slug":"mark-buttigieg","vote":"no"},{"name":"Natalie Ward","person_id":"nsw_2236","person_slug":"natalie-ward","vote":"paired"},{"name":"Natasha Maclaren-Jones","person_id":"nsw_88","person_slug":"natasha-maclaren-jones","vote":"paired"},{"name":"Nichole Overall","person_id":"nsw_2266","person_slug":"nichole-overall","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Penny Sharpe","person_id":"nsw_28","person_slug":"penny-sharpe","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Primrose","person_id":"nsw_3","person_slug":"peter-primrose","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Merton","person_id":"nsw_2304","person_slug":"rachel-merton","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Robert Borsak","person_id":"nsw_54","person_slug":"robert-borsak","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rose Jackson","person_id":"nsw_2258","person_slug":"rose-jackson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Kaine","person_id":"nsw_2296","person_slug":"sarah-kaine","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Mitchell","person_id":"nsw_93","person_slug":"sarah-mitchell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Barrett","person_id":"nsw_2262","person_slug":"scott-barrett","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Farlow","person_id":"nsw_122","person_slug":"scott-farlow","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Lawrence","person_id":"nsw_2297","person_slug":"stephen-lawrence","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Higginson","person_id":"nsw_2268","person_slug":"sue-higginson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Susan Carter","person_id":"nsw_2302","person_slug":"susan-carter","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tara Moriarty","person_id":"nsw_2250","person_slug":"tara-moriarty","vote":"paired"},{"name":"Wes Fang","person_id":"nsw_2232","person_slug":"wes-fang","vote":"aye"}],"name":"National Park Estate (Great Koala National Park Reservations) Bill 2026","noes":18,"question":"That distinction matters for clubs trying to plan responsibly. An organiser who identifies a safer or more suitable route should be able to have that proposal assessed. A statutory rule tied to the commencement date can prevent the approval process from considering whether the alternative would produce a better result. Removing this subsection does not compel the Minister to approve a race. The other considerations remain, including natural and cultural values, public and participant safety, environmental risks, and relevant guidelines. The Minister can still impose conditions or refuse a proposal. As with amendment No. 5, the five named regional park exclusions also remain. Members should not describe this amendment as removing every restriction on motorsport or guaranteeing unrestricted vehicle access. It removes one particular prohibition within the motor race approval scheme. It also does not itself authorise someone to build a road or start driving through reserved land. What it does is remove the rule that an approval under this section can only permit vehicle use on a road that predates commencement. That allows the approval decision to address the proposal actually put forward.","result":"negative","slug":"division-nsw-lc-2026-10-22-12","source_url":"https://api.parliament.nsw.gov.au/api/hansard/search/daily/fragment/HANSARD-1820781676-106209"}
